Mining in ''Human Host'' is more than resource-gathering. Because '''all terrain is destructible''', mining is how you dig tunnels, level building sites, and create underground bases.

== How it works ==

Point at any terrain surface with a Pickaxe equipped and swing. Each hit removes a small volume of terrain and yields materials based on what you dug:

* '''Grass / dirt''': no yield, but flattens the terrain
* '''Sand''': yields Sand (desert biomes)
* '''Stone''': yields Stone
* '''Ore veins''': yields the ore plus some Stone

The internal system is driven by <code>Terrain_Dig.Dig_Terrain(RaycastHit, bool, bool)</code> and a material lookup table (<code>Skill_Mgr._MinerSoundMats</code>) that maps each terrain material to a sound and a possible ore yield.

== Ore and mineral catalog ==

The addressables catalog lists sixteen mineable rock and ore assets. Prefix <code>BO_</code> = "Build Ore" (the placeable mineable-block form).

